INCOMPLETE -- THE FULL LICENCE TEXT MUST REPLACE THIS NOTICE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The paragraphs above are the copyright notice the GPL asks you to attach. They
are NOT the licence. Distributing GPL software requires the complete text of
GPL-3.0 to travel with it, and that text is about 35,000 characters which
should be copied from the canonical source rather than retyped.

The reliable way, in the GitHub web interface:

    Add file  ->  Create new file  ->  name it LICENSE  ->  "Choose a license
    template"  ->  GNU General Public License v3.0

That inserts the canonical text. Paste the copyright notice above back at the
top afterwards, or leave GitHub's own header.

Or from a terminal:

    curl -o LICENSE https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.txt

Until that is done this file is a placeholder and the repository is not
correctly licensed.
